{"id": "AS-01", "dimension": "broad_synthesis", "question": "What does 21 CFR 820.10 require?", "answer_raw": "21 CFR 820.10 requires manufacturers to document a quality management system that complies with ISO 13485 and other applicable requirements, as well as comply with the listed ISO 13485 Clauses. The requirements include (a) documenting the system to assign unique device identification, (b) documenting traceability procedures, (c) notifying the FDA of complaints, and (d) handling advisory notices in accordance with part 806. Additionally, manufacturers must comply with design and development requirements for class II, class III, and class I devices, as appropriate. The enforcement of these requirements is outlined in part 803 and 806.", "answer_final": "21 CFR 820.10 requires manufacturers to document a quality management system that complies with ISO 13485 and other applicable requirements, as well as comply with the listed ISO 13485 Clauses. The requirements include (a) documenting the system to assign unique device identification, (b) documenting traceability procedures, (c) notifying the FDA of complaints, and (d) handling advisory notices in accordance with part 806. Additionally, manufacturers must comply with design and development requirements for class II, class III, and class I devices, as appropriate. The enforcement of these requirements is outlined in part 803 and 806.", "answer_shape": {"mode": "synthesis", "scope": "section", "exhaustive": false, "requested_units": ["21 CFR 820.10"], "focus_terms": [], "signals": [], "rationale": "an overview of 21 CFR 820.10"}, "evidence_plan": {"mode": "synthesis", "lead_in": [1], "groups": [{"key": "820.10(a)", "label": "21 CFR 820.10(a)", "heading": "Document", "kind": "requirement", "head": 2, "members": [2], "items": [], "requirement_ids": ["r1"]}, {"key": "820.10(b)", "label": "21 CFR 820.10(b)", "heading": "Applicable regulatory requirements", "kind": "requirement", "head": 3, "members": [3, 4, 5, 6, 7]